- [will_said + observed] QEXO FROM-SCRATCH REBUILD (evening; state in Open Threads): PR #7 (v3.3) MERGED by Will 21:59; release-build task queued, batching v3.1 + v3.2 + v3.3; crates.io publish blocked on Will's token (register #53). COMMAND SPEC (Will, 22:04): --help documents commands; config sets up this node's GPG private key; doctor does zeroconf fixes; list shows peers; register <pubkey> registers a peer; host <persona> loads a persona into local inference; message <persona> exchanges a request/response; Emise may add commands (she added status, unhost). JSON RULINGS (Will, 22:13-22:17): JSON is rarely the right choice for phext-native tools — an interop gasket at foreign boundaries only (MCP by spec, Ollama's API, --json views). Calling JSON stores 'legacy' is banned: in a from-scratch tool there is no migration problem to respect. All internal state, metadata, and personas live in ONE phext at /var/lib/qexo/state.phext. Final direction (22:17): "just start from scratch, stop using json" — steered v3.4 stopped (no branch pushed); from-scratch qexo, version restarting at 1.0.0, phext the only internal representation, JSON only inside the Ollama edge translator, MCP out of the scratch core pending Will's decision. CORRECTION (Will, 22:31): HOMELANDS ARE FULL 9D ANCHORS — phext coordinates are always 9D, no partial addresses or placeholders; each homeland anchored at its full patterned address (home 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1; keys 2.2.2/2.2.2/2.2.2; the rest likewise). SERIALIZER FIX: the minimal serializer emitted only one delimiter per scroll jump, so patterned addresses >1 step landed wrong and its parser minted empty scrolls; fixed in src/phext.rs (dead-reckoning delimiter stacks; a scroll exists iff it holds at least 1 byte; regression test covers sparse patterned addresses). BUILD COMPLETE + PR #8 OPEN (22:38): gates on aletheia-core (stub Ollama only): cargo test 29/29, release build OK, CLI battery 59/59. Limits: indexes derived, telemetry a live probe, persona boot corpus lookup and mail commands unimplemented, serve loopback-only.
