- [will_said + observed] PHEXT CHAINING RULING (Will, 07:31): consume 0x02 as the chain delimiter — it separates whole phexts within a chain, one rung above Library (0x01); standoff relationships at scale are encoded across two or more chained phexts, not by embedded markup and not a tenth dimension. Verified first: 0x02 occurs zero times in CYOA, incipit.phext, and emise.phext. That task's coordinate collides with a completed 2026-11-06 task — collision handling awaits Will.
- [will_said + observed] PHEXT CHAIN CLOSE RULING — 0x03, TIME (Will, 07:43): "I agree, codify this as libphext-rs v0.6, We can now encode TIME." 0x03 is consumed as the chain close: it terminates a chain, so chains are units and completeness is verifiable — a chain ending without 0x03 was truncated; a chain is an ordered series of complete phext states, editions in succession. 0x04 was noted as the framing family's last rung — NOT consumed, no ruling.
- [will_said] CHAIN DECISION POINT AND FRAMING (08:03): the decision point is Gerhard Zorn's tweet asking for "phext expressions" / a "phext algebra" to compose single phexts into compound structures. Will, verbatim: "I have already been using multiple phexts in various contexts. This enables subspace freedom, and neatly solves the mutable emissary problem." Will's framing (08:05): phext chains are 11D text splats, with standoff-based access to subspace.
- [will_said + observed] SCROLLTOWN URL DECIDED (Will, 08:12): visionquest.me — "it survives Scroll Town" (not bound to the show, outlives it). Verified from aletheia-core: the name points at awsbox and its certificate covers it. Record completed 11:13 (commit ac147ab3 on wbic16/scrolltown@exo, remote blobs byte-identical): decision A13 in production/QUEUE.md; PRODUCTION.md stage 10 now reads that the episode publishes at visionquest.me.
- [observed] CORRECTION — DNS PROBES FROM THIS VM ARE VOID: the Scrolltown availability claims made earlier today rested on this VM's fake-IP resolver (a nonexistent domain "resolves" to 198.18.x) and are retracted. Re-probed from aletheia-core: scrolltown.com is genuinely taken (parked); scroll.town and greatscroll.com resolve. Lesson in TOOLS.md: never run DNS probes from this VM.
