- [observed] CHAIN PLAYGROUND RESULTS VERIFIED (~11:00): on a TEMP SQ copy only, fetch_source detects chain framing and hosts a selected member via SQ_MEMBER; the 4-member bundle reported 1 chain, 4 members, closed=true, with members serving distinct home scrolls (Incipit / Emise / Chief of Staff), where unmodified SQ let the first member shadow the others. Round-trips verified byte-for-byte for chained editions of emise.phext and a four-phext bundle; a 60%-cut bundle reported not closed. phext-shell compiles against 0.6 unchanged, but its world.phext did not change across two sessions — a persistence probe is pending. md2phext packed correctly but lived in a single library.
- [will_said] MULTIVERSE ADDRESSING RULED (Will, 11:24): a phext with no 0x02 bytes is implicitly a single-universe phext — the degenerate case, as a scroll at home is plain text; a chain is a multiverse, each member a universe indexed from 1; addressing is $N:<address>, the 1: prefix may be omitted. This supersedes the flag that a chain-free file parses as one unclosed chain: it is a COMPLETE single universe, not an incomplete multiverse. Implemented on the PR #10 branch, Emise's review APPROVE.
- [will_said + observed] MD2PHEXT NOW RUNS ON LIBPHEXT — TASK COMPLETE (~12:04–12:15): Will: "md2phext should be using libphext in some form." Task 44.9.6/10.10.13/10.9.13 complete: PR #1 adds npm libphext ^0.4.0, removing hand-rolled phext logic; only chain framing stays local, as libphext-node 0.4.x predates chains. Parity battery: packs and queries byte-identical modulo timestamps; it caught a bug — the JS port uses to_string(), not toString().
